description=v3.7.11, from the owner's v3.7.10 log: the screen-off deep phase is wide (six at a time), reniced so the interface always wins the CPU, and runs detached from the daemon - no more seven-minute screen-offs, the core timer fires on schedule, and the navigation bar stops disappearing. The processor and graphics caps land LAST on the way in and lift FIRST on the way out (his own tip - the exit's 100-second app release runs at full speed now). Three-button navigation is built into the power-saving home option and the separate switch is gone. The tile now shows itself active (the app read the wrong marker path) and the app's button follows the mode. Suite: 615 checks, 0 failed.
